Z||000009||ChadMan||08-20-99||07:11 AM||||I'd have to agree with Kel and DXR_DAD.  The fastbacks are cool and I've always liked the lines of the base coupes, but the aero notchbacks (85 GT, 86-7 SE) are the best-looking, especially with monochrome paint.<p>There was a guy at the Nationals selling a maroon 87 SE in good shape with T-tops (!) for $2500 OBO.  The catch: it was a 4-banger.  Still, it made me go all gooey in the knees thinking about the engine-swap possibilities.  My wife had to lead me away by the nose before I bought yet another Fiero.
